From edfec6bf239e440f9313e8be127f5a46dcf65daa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:15:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] httpd, www: a page token on every apply, cross-site checks,
 secrets out of page source (102.8 line)

2026-11-03 review.
- Every authenticated page carries a hook that adds the per-boot http_id to each form, XHR and
  fetch aimed at start_apply*.htm, apply.cgi or applyapp.cgi; a browser apply without it is
  refused. Not asked of the ASUS app or scripts, a pristine-stock UI (reaper_inject=0) or an
  AiMesh node; a page served before login never carries the token.
- The browser cross-site refusal applies on the HTTPS listener too, and to start_autodet.asp,
  ajax_trigger_chk_sta.asp and apscan.asp. The IPsec upload sets ipsec_profile_item only.
- Range: one parser for the headers and the body, 206 with Content-Range; a file of unknown size
  is sent whole.
- get_file_md5() and findasus keep names to their own characters; the repeater-mode SSID is
  escaped.
- The RADIUS secrets, the dashboard's WPS PIN and the MLO password are no longer printed into page
  source (presence flags; read on Show).
- Analytics probe / save / test are POST bodies; the LAN CSV export guards formula cells; the
  password page's username is a JS literal; the Firmware page's node button; AiMesh AP-mode names
  are encoded on the way in.
- On an HTTPS-only GUI the plain-HTTP instance (run for Gatekeeper's waiting page) sends every
  other request to HTTPS before any login.
- gencert.sh: keys and the certificate archive are private from the start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
